      "order": 0,
      "content": "<div class=\"mm-release-marker\" data-mm-release=\"f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605\" data-mm-topic=\"t-mm-10-026\" hidden></div>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21090]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: \"Calibri Light\", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt'>3.15.  </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: \"Calibri Light\", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt'>PREVIOUS C/S</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21091]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Discuss:</strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21092]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Risks and benefits of VBAC vs C/S </span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21093]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Vaginal birth is associated with a small chance of uterine rupture instrumental birth.</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21094]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Emergency C/S has higher chance of heavy </span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21095]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>bleeding needing blood transfusion, infection, Complications in future pregnancies, longer hospital stay.</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21096]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Little difference of outcome of baby in VBAC vs C/S</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21097]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Support full range of analgesia</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21098]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Regional analgesia increases chances of instrumental birth but reduces chances of another C/S</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21099]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>No need of continuous CTG and routine amniotomy.</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[21100]\">\u00a0</p>",
      "content_sha256": "26df8467f8eb232cc9214638fb7c1a526f6ad3aa0cfefb0b40d8d1a2c7d99efb",
